<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Uaymil</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A thinly documented Maya province of south-eastern Yucatán, conquered with great brutality by the Spanish in the 1540s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Uaymil emerged after the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441 in the south-east of the peninsula, between the provinces of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cochuah">Cochuah</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chetumal">Chetumal</a>, in what is now southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a>. Little is known of its origins.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It appears to have been a loose grouping of towns in a region of lagoons and forest, known only from a few colonial sources. Its people farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and probably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a> and took part in coastal trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1544 the Spanish captains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspar-pacheco">Gaspar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melchor-pacheco">Melchor Pacheco</a> conquered Uaymil and its neighbours with exceptional cruelty, and the region was largely depopulated. It became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:88.38%;width:2.05%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uaymil province</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=uaymil" aria-label="Uaymil on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2243 1421 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Uaymil lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2563 1677L2591 1670M2563 1677L4910 989M2563 1677L2590 1658"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2591 1670h0M4910 989h0M2590 1658h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2563 1677h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2563 1677h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=uaymil">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
